borderline (3.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rewrite rule optimization into bounded phases with dependency tracking.
  * Preserve pushed guards, non-terminal inputs, temporary-chain call semantics
    and named user-chain extension points.
  * Preserve effect order and multiplicity, and compare flags and constants
    correctly during optimization.
  * Improve profitable factoring, caller specialization, rule merging and
    terminal-tail sharing; order pure jumps by outcome and callee cost.
  * Merge disjoint jumps to the same read-only chain while preserving effect
    order and multiplicity.
  * Allow profitable predicate factoring across two consecutive rules.
  * Reduce IP predicates using source and destination zone address domains,
    including zones restricted to a single address family.
  * Prefer equivalent positive predicates when their cost is identical.
  * Fix IPv4 and IPv6 IP-set union, difference, intersection and equality,
    including splitting the IPv4 universe into both halves.
  * Improve large IP-set construction and subtraction complexity, and coalesce
    adjacent prefixes in unions.
  * Preserve optimized predicate order in nftables output and emit zero for
    empty TCP flag bitmasks.
  * Match singleton loopback interface predicates by interface index instead
    of name.
  * Improve IANA-based packet validation, private-network filtering and
    expansion of local and global zone address ranges.
  * Correct local/global zone aliases and omit address classifiers for
    address families without configured networks.
  * Correct source and destination addresses in DHCPv6 server request rules.
  * Generate service aliases without colliding with protocol definitions and
    use the canonical imap service name in the example configuration.
  * Expand optimizer and IP-set regression coverage; remove test dependencies
    on host service entries and autogenerated configuration files.
  * Check SysV init script syntax without executing service logic during tests.
  * Warn and retry without nft optimization when optimized rule validation fails.
  * Preserve startup failure exit statuses and clean up temporary rules and logs.
  * Update CI actions and manage Dune caching separately.
  * Require Menhir >= 20180523 and add the ppx_expect test dependency.
  * Improve nft rule formatting.

 -- Anders Peter Fugmann <anders@fugmann.net>  Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:08:55 +0100

